# Build context for standin/, harness/ and facade/ Dockerfiles (context is the repository root).
#
# Deny everything, then allow only what the images copy: the root build props,
# contracts/, the three component directories and the stand-in seed files.
# Later lines override earlier ones, so build output and per-run data are
# re-excluded after the allow lines; images always restore and build from a clean tree.
#
# baseline/, RESULTS.md, docker-compose.yml and .env reach the harness at run time
# through the .:/repo bind mount and are never part of an image. Everything else
# under Erewhon/ (schemas, .NET projects) stays out of the context.

*

!Directory.Packages.props
!Erewhon.Strangler.props
!contracts/
!standin/
!harness/
!facade/
!Erewhon/DataFiles/

# .git and *.pdf are already excluded by '*'; they stay explicit so a future
# relaxation of '*' cannot admit them. bin/, obj/ and artifacts/ must follow the
# allow lines so local build output and per-run data inside them never enter.
.git
**/bin
**/obj
artifacts/
**/artifacts
*.pdf
